<div class="well"><strong>Median Family Incomes</strong></div>

<ul>
<li>FY 2021 Median Income Methodology in <a href="/portal/datasets/il/il21/Medians-Methodology-FY21.pdf"><strong>pdf</strong></a>
</li>
 <li>Notice on Median Family Incomes for FY 2021, State Median Family Incomes in  <a href="/portal/datasets/il/il21/Medians2021.pdf"><strong>pdf</strong></a>
</li>
</ul>
<br/>


<div class="well"><strong>State Income Limits and Median Family Incomes</strong></div>

<ul>
  <li>To view the FY 2021 State 30%, 50% and 80% Income Limits (based on median family incomes without adjustments made to HUD Income Limits), please  <a href="/portal/datasets/il/il21/State-Incomelimits-Report-FY21.pdf"><strong>click here</strong></a>. </li>

</ul>
<br/>



<div class="well"><strong>HUD 30% Income Limit for ALL Areas</strong></div>

<p>These are 30% Income Limits, calculated with high and low housing cost adjustments, state non-metropolitan minimum but without the increases for poverty guidelines in the Section 8 Extremely Low Family Incomes</p>
<ul>
<li> Tables for HUD 30% Income Limits (in <a href="/portal/datasets/il/il21/IncomeLimits-30-FY21.pdf"><strong>pdf</strong></a>)</li>
<li> Tables for HUD 30% Income Limits (in <a href="/portal/datasets/il/il21/HUD-IL-NPG-FY21.xlsx"><strong>EXCEL</strong></a>)</li>
  </ul>

<br/>

								</div>
														
