																					<div class="tab-pane fade active in show" id="data_Revised-1999" role="tabpanel">
									<p><strong>The changes made relate only to the Section 8 Existing "30 percent of area median income" limits</strong>. These income limits have been increased wherever necessary to ensure that the one-person 30 percent income limit is at least as high as the State Supplemental Security Income (SSI) benefit level.</p>

<p>Effective July 21,1999</p>

<p> <A HREF="/portal/datasets/il/fmr99rev/REVISED-FY-1999-SECTION-8-INCOME-LIMITS.docx">Click here</A> to download the nationwide copy of this file in WORD format. </p>

<p><a href="/portal/datasets/il/fmr99rev/REV99-30percent.pdf">Click here</a> to learn about the changes to the 30% income limits made on July 21, 1999 (Notice PDR-99-04). </p>

<P> <A HREF ="/portal/datasets/il/fmr99rev/Rev-FY99-30percent.xls">Click here</a> download the FY 1999 Income Limits in Excel format.</p><br>

								</div>
														
